From 683b54595e9adae47bcd61fe2bd3149412bf1f3c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MikolajQ <mikolaj.q@wp.pl>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 10:16:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] NfcService: Don't poll with the screen off on NCI 1.0
 controllers

Commit 3e8c123a5 ("Enabling all discovery techs in case of screen
locked state.") lowered NFC_POLLING_MODE to SCREEN_STATE_OFF_UNLOCKED,
so polling stays enabled in every screen state. That relies on the
NCI 2.0 power sub-states: doSetScreenState() then sets
CON_DISCOVERY_PARAM to disable polling while the screen is off.

doSetScreenState() returns early on NCI 1.0 controllers, so nothing
ever turns polling off and the controller keeps running the full
poll loop with the screen off. On a Samsung Galaxy A50s (PN547) the
controller then requests its clock every ~540 ms, which wakes the AP
about twice a second (223k wakeups / 35 h, ~90 mA standby drain).

Keep the previous threshold (SCREEN_STATE_ON_UNLOCKED) for controllers
older than NCI 2.0. NCI 2.0 behaviour is unchanged.

Test: A50s (PN547, NCI 1.0), screen off: RF_DISCOVER drops to NFC-A
      listen only and the nfc_clk wakeups go from ~220 to 0 per minute.
      Screen on and unlocked: RF_DISCOVER carries the poll techs as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Dr8X39PngEfThUaxTxyj9B
Change-Id: Ib7f0e5cf249e3cecda6764c76237cc0e27572890
---
 NfcNci/src/com/android/nfc/NfcService.java | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/NfcNci/src/com/android/nfc/NfcService.java b/NfcNci/src/com/android/nfc/NfcService.java
index 9dc6a3c..46dc7a2 100644
--- a/NfcNci/src/com/android/nfc/NfcService.java
+++ b/NfcNci/src/com/android/nfc/NfcService.java
@@ -311,6 +311,9 @@ public class NfcService implements DeviceHostListener, ForegroundUtils.Callback
 
     // minimum screen state that enables NFC polling
     static final int NFC_POLLING_MODE = ScreenStateHelper.SCREEN_STATE_OFF_UNLOCKED;
+    // NCI 1.0 controllers have no power sub-states, so polling enabled here is never turned off
+    // by doSetScreenState() and keeps running with the screen off.
+    static final int NFC_POLLING_MODE_NCI_1_0 = ScreenStateHelper.SCREEN_STATE_ON_UNLOCKED;
 
     // Time to wait for NFC controller to initialize before watchdog
     // goes off. This time is chosen large, because firmware download
@@ -5098,7 +5101,9 @@ public class NfcService implements DeviceHostListener, ForegroundUtils.Callback
         // Recompute discovery parameters based on screen state
         NfcDiscoveryParameters.Builder paramsBuilder = NfcDiscoveryParameters.newBuilder();
         // Polling
-        if (screenState >= NFC_POLLING_MODE && isReaderOptionEnabled()) {
+        int pollingMode =
+                (nci_version < NCI_VERSION_2_0) ? NFC_POLLING_MODE_NCI_1_0 : NFC_POLLING_MODE;
+        if (screenState >= pollingMode && isReaderOptionEnabled()) {
             // Check if reader-mode is enabled
             if (mReaderModeParams != null) {
                 int techMask = 0;
